<AnchorPane maxHeight="-Infinity" maxWidth="-Infinity" minHeight="-Infinity" minWidth="-Infinity" prefHeight="750.0" prefWidth="600.0" styleClass="root-background" stylesheets="@../css_files/readmeMdTutorial.css" xmlns="http://javafx.com/javafx/26" xmlns:fx="http://javafx.com/fxml/1">
   <children>
      <TextArea editable="false" layoutX="222.0" layoutY="30.0" prefHeight="200.0" prefWidth="200.0" styleClass="text-area" text="# HOW_TO_PLAY.md&#10;&#10;## Welcome to ParadigmBreach&#10;&#10;You are **C1pher**, and your goal is to break through the defenses of the **Paradigm Wardens**. Along the way, you will answer quiz questions and solve programming problems. You are not alone: your AI companion, **Pengu**, is here to help.&#10;&#10;Read this file once and you're ready to play.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## 1. Your Desktop&#10;&#10;When the game starts, you'll see a desktop with app icons.&#10;&#10;|        Icon        |                   What it does                   |&#10;|--------------------|--------------------------------------------------|&#10;|    **Terminal**    | Opens the command-line where the game is played. |&#10;| **HOW_TO_PLAY.md** |                   This guide.                    |&#10;&#10;**Controls:** the mouse is all you need on the desktop.&#10;&#10;- **Single-click** an icon to select it.&#10;- **Double-click** an icon to open it.&#10;&#10;&gt; **Tip:** You can leave this guide open in its own window while you play.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## 2. Your Goal&#10;&#10;Answer every question correctly to clear each stage. Clear them all, face the Paradigm Wardens, and finish the game.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## 3. How to Answer a Question&#10;&#10;1. Open the **Terminal**.&#10;2. A question and its choices will appear on the screen.&#10;3. Click the **input line** at the bottom (the line that starts with `&gt;`).&#10;4. **Type your answer** and press **Enter**.&#10;&#10;```&#10;Which keyword is used to inherit from a class in Java?&#10;&#10;  A) implements&#10;  B) extends&#10;  C) inherits&#10;  D) super&#10;&#10;&gt; B&#10;```&#10;&#10;You don't need a special command to answer. Just type your answer and press Enter.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## 4. Meet Pengu&#10;&#10;**Pengu** is C1pher's AI companion. Stuck on a question? Ask Pengu for help by typing a command in the terminal.&#10;&#10;&gt; **Warning:** Pengu is a homebrew AI model, so he can **hallucinate**. He only has a **50% chance** of giving the correct answer. Trust him at your own risk!&#10;&#10;### Two ways to get help&#10;&#10;#### Peek: &quot;What do you think, Pengu?&quot;&#10;&#10;```&#10;pngu -ask&#10;```&#10;&#10;Pengu tells you what he thinks the answer is. **You decide** whether to follow his advice or ignore it.&#10;&#10;- Costs **1 Pengu Token**.&#10;- Safe to use: you still choose your own answer.&#10;&#10;#### Copy: &quot;Just answer for me, Pengu!&quot;&#10;&#10;```&#10;pngu -answer&#10;```&#10;&#10;Pengu answers the question **for you**, whether he's right or wrong.&#10;&#10;- **Costs no tokens.**&#10;- Use it every time you like, even when you're out of tokens.&#10;- Risky: there is a 50% chance the answer is wrong, and you can't take it back.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## 5. Pengu Tokens&#10;&#10;| Rule | Details |&#10;|------|---------|&#10;| You start each stage with | **2 Pengu Tokens** |&#10;| `pngu -ask` costs | **1 token** |&#10;| `pngu -answer` costs | **Nothing** |&#10;| Tokens reset | To **2** at the start of every new stage |&#10;&#10;**Strategy tips**&#10;&#10;- Tokens do not carry over, so use them freely before a stage ends.&#10;- Save `pngu -answer` for questions where you have no idea and no tokens left.&#10;- `pngu -ask` gives you a second opinion, but Pengu is still wrong half the time. Use your own knowledge too.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## 6. Terminal Commands&#10;&#10;| Command | What it does |&#10;|---------|--------------|&#10;| `help` | Shows all available commands. |&#10;| `clear` | Clears the text on the screen. |&#10;| `exit` | Closes the terminal window. |&#10;| `pngu -ask` | Peek at what Pengu thinks (1 token). |&#10;| `pngu -answer` | Let Pengu answer for you (free). |&#10;&#10;Commands are not case-sensitive, so `HELP` and `help` work the same.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## 7. Paradigm Wardens&#10;&#10;Before you face a Paradigm Warden, a **cutscene** will play. It will brief you on the story and any new mechanics, so watch it. After you defeat the Wardens, the ending sequence begins.&#10;&#10;---&#10;&#10;## Quick Recap&#10;&#10;1. **Double-click** the Terminal icon.&#10;2. **Read** the question.&#10;3. **Type** your answer, then press **Enter**.&#10;4. Stuck? Type `pngu -ask` (uses 1 of your 2 tokens) or `pngu -answer` (free, 50% risky).&#10;5. Clear the stage, get your tokens reset, repeat.&#10;&#10;**Good luck, C1pher. Break the paradigm.**&#10;" wrapText="true" AnchorPane.bottomAnchor="20.0" AnchorPane.leftAnchor="20.0" AnchorPane.rightAnchor="20.0" AnchorPane.topAnchor="20.0">
